      "pronunciationText": "Let's measure some slopes on this middle piece. At zero, the height is zero and the slope is one. At pi over four, the height is one and the slope is two. At pi over three, the height is root three, about one point seven three, and the slope is four. Look at the pattern. Height zero, slope one. Height one, slope two. Height root three, slope four. Each slope is one more than the height squared. On the beach, the slope is how fast the spot moves as the beam turns. It's slowest straight in front, and the further along the spot is, the faster it races. Hold on to that, because the algebra is about to explain it."
    },
